## 🔨 go build — Compile
```bash
go build [-o output] [flags] [packages]
```
- Ignores `*_test.go` during build
- Output name derived from package or first `.go` file
- `-o <path>` = set output file/directory

**Common Flags** (shared: build, clean, get, install, list, run, test):
| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `-C dir` | Change directory first (must be 1st) |
| `-a` | Rebuild all, even up-to-date |
| `-n` | Show commands — don't run |
| `-p N` | Parallel jobs (default = GOMAXPROCS) |
| `-race` | Enable race detector |
| `-cover` | Instrument coverage |
| `-v` | Print package names |
| `-x` | Print all executed commands |
| `-tags a,b` | Set build tags |
| `-trimpath` | Strip absolute paths from binary |
| `-mod readonly\|vendor\|mod` | Module resolution mode |
| `-ldflags '...'` | Pass args to linker |
| `-gcflags '...'` | Pass args to compiler |
| `-pgo auto\|off\|file` | Profile-guided optimization |
| `-buildvcs true\|false\|auto` | Stamp Git info into binary |

