## 📥 go get — Manage Dependencies
```bash
go get example.com/pkg              # add/latest
go get example.com/pkg@v1.2.3       # specific version
go get example.com/pkg@none         # remove dependency
go get -u ./...                      # update all deps
go get -u=patch ./...                # patch updates only
```
- `-t` = also update test dependencies
- Updates `go.mod` + downloads source to module cache

---

## 📦 go install — Install Binaries
```bash
go install ./cmd/mytool
go install example.com/cmd@latest   # versioned, ignores local go.mod
```
- Output → `$GOBIN` (default: `~/go/bin`)
- Versioned installs useful for CLI tools without touching project deps

---

## 📋 go list — Query / Scripting
```bash
go list ./...                        # list all packages
go list -m all                       # list all modules
go list -f '{{.ImportPath}}' ./...  # custom format
go list -json ./...                  # machine-readable
go list -deps ./pkg                  # list deps recursively
```

---

## ✅ go test — Run Tests
```bash
go test ./...
go test -v -run TestName ./...       # verbose + filter
go test -cover ./...                 # show coverage
go test -race ./...                  # with race detector
```

---

## 🧹 go clean — Remove Build Artifacts
```bash
go clean -cache           # clear build cache
go clean -modcache        # clear downloaded modules
go clean -testcache       # expire test results
go clean -r ./...         # recurse + remove binaries
```

---

## ⚙️ go env — Environment
```bash
go env                    # print all
go env GOMOD GOBIN        # specific vars
go env -w GOBIN=~/bin     # persist setting
go env -u GOBIN           # unset custom
go env -changed           # show non-default only
```

---

## 📖 go doc — Documentation
```bash
go doc                    # current package
go doc encoding/json
go doc json.Number
go doc -all .             # everything in current pkg
go doc -http=:6060        # serve HTML docs
```

---

## 📜 go generate — Code Generation
```bash
go generate ./...
go generate -run "proto" ./...  # run matching directives only
```
- Scans for: `//go:generate command args...`
- Sets: `$GOFILE`, `$GOPACKAGE`, `$GOOS`, `$GOARCH`…

